I'm a long time MMO player since EQ1 and played or at least tried every mmo out there since then. Lately i was really bored as no game was really cutting it for me. I hated minecraft, it wasn't for me, so Trove was the only mmo of the recent released mmo's i didn't try and i was certain i would hate.
I picked it up out of boredom and i'm so happy i did because this is the best game i played for ages.
It is brilliant, very well made, very simple to start but very deep and complicated to master all the aspects. The tutorial Quest and the first starting levels are very well crafted and you get the hang of things very Quickly.
Gameplay wise, it plays as an action mmo, there is no tab targeting and the game is very fast paced during fights. There is a lot of class's and they all have a different feel to them so it's pretty awsome. Every class have 3 spells and an auto attack the mechanics aren't very complicated but the costumisation of the gear is where this game shine (magic damage, physical, jump, stability, knockback, health regen, magic find, etc etc). You can really min max a lot of stuff and get very creative with you'r gear builds)
This is a sandbox game, you can build/craft basicly everything. There is no set path, you can build, take up Quests and Adventures, do group content, solo content, Farm materials, invest in you'r cornerstone (house) invest in you'r club (guild world totally buildable), it's up to you. You can also farm in group or solo.  There is a thousand stuff to do in the game and it doesnt feel grindy at all as everything you do get's rewarding very fast.
The Store have everything you could need but the game provides you with ways to get what the store is selling for free. I dont feel puched to buy anything and everything i need to progress is available to be crafted or obtained through gameplay so it's really there as an option to speed up you'r advancement.
- Pros :
- Very fun;
- Not repetitive;
- Fast paced;
- If you are slightly creative you will have a blast;
- Tones of content;
- Crafting and farming is pretty well done;
- The tutorial is well done
- Combat and class's are super fun
- Many Daily ''Ups'' to take advantage of like double the ore, double gathering, double the shards, double the loot etc. etc.
- Cons :
- So far i honestly don't find any It's either you like it or not as for the rest all the systems are very well designed. If you can get past the cubic graphics, you will have a blast.
I totally recommend this game.

